body:
@kucharskimaciej 

Not sure if it is because `bind` is deprecated. Have you tried using `provide`?

```
import {bootstrap, provide} from 'angular2/angular2';
import {
    ROUTER_PROVIDERS,
    APP_BASE_HREF,
    ROUTER_PRIMARY_COMPONENT
} from 'angular2/router';

const ROUTER_CONFIG = [
    ROUTER_PROVIDERS,
    provide(APP_BASE_HREF, {useValue:'/'}),
    provide(ROUTER_PRIMARY_COMPONENT, {useValue: RootComponent})
];
```

Yup, `provide` gives the same result.

See this code:
`src/code/dom/browser_adapter.ts`

``` javascript
var baseElement = null;
function getBaseElementHref(): string {
  if (isBlank(baseElement)) {
    baseElement = document.querySelector('base');
    if (isBlank(baseElement)) {
      return null;
    }
  }
  return baseElement.getAttribute('href');
}
```

Which is used by this function in the same file:

``` javascript
getBaseHref(): string {
    var href = getBaseElementHref();
    if (isBlank(href)) {
      return null;
    }
    return relativePath(href);
  }
```

As you can see, if there is no base element, the `getBaseHref()` function will always return a `null`. The value is then used in `PathLocationStrategy` constructor:

``` javascript
export class PathLocationStrategy extends LocationStrategy {
  private _location: Location;
  private _history: History;
  private _baseHref: string;

  constructor() {
    super();
    this._location = DOM.getLocation();
    this._history = DOM.getHistory();
    this._baseHref = DOM.getBaseHref();
  }
...
```

Therefore if there is no base element, the `_baseHref` property will be a `null`. It is then used in this function:

``` javascript
prepareExternalUrl(internal: string): string { return this._baseHref + internal; }
```

And this is used by `router-link` directive:

``` javascript
  set routeParams(changes: any[]) {
    this._routeParams = changes;
    this._navigationInstruction = this._router.generate(this._routeParams);

    var navigationHref = stringifyInstruction(this._navigationInstruction);
    this.visibleHref = this._location.prepareExternalUrl(navigationHref);
  }
```

And the `visibleHref` property is bound to the `router-link` element `href` attribute:

``` javascript
@Directive({
  selector: '[router-link]',
  inputs: ['routeParams: routerLink'],
  host: {
    '(click)': 'onClick()',
    '[attr.href]': 'visibleHref',
    '[class.router-link-active]': 'isRouteActive'
  }
})
```

And since `null + "/hello" === "null/hello"` - wrong link :)

BTW. is there a guide somewhere how to build angular2 source? I think I'll be able to fix this issue myself, but i want to be sure it works ;)
